1. Meanwhile, Germany's defense minister visited Budapest to ramp up defense and military ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen, Audi to recall almost 1 million cars in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3afe90e2bf2ce8e79d82a0a7568fcad19f79949e7303f3919cc7399a2213129</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-audi-to-recall-almost-1-million-cars-in-germany/a-79426960--b707dbde3045.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-audi-to-recall-almost-1-million-cars-in-germany/a-79426960?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volkswagen and its subsidiary Audi are to recall nearly a million vehicles in Germany due to a potential steering fault.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a95d71cec97524ca9fb4fc795b37aeaeee8c221d569cb2d590a647ffd4482df1</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin officially withdraws Olympics bid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6daf9cf57f2dd6a5c2dea987ed8b4811308d0f04f40e147bfe6d37c30e665ad6</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294--30622a12ce08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-officially-withdraws-olympics-bid/live-79406294?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's decision to withdraw its Olympic bid means that only Munich and the western Rhine/Ruhr region are left in the running as potential Olympic hosts. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD, CDU ban new Holocaust 'stumbling stones' in Heidenau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:153e3b37150fd35aeaa7a642d751f99a65361fd242a99f21ee620a9ac3371a87</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919--bafd061ca07a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-cdu-ban-new-holocaust-stumbling-stones-in-heidenau/a-79433919?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Activists, politicians and representatives of Holocaust victims reacted with anger after the center-right CDU party joined forces with the AfD to ban new Stolpersteine (stumbling stones) in the eastern town of Heidenau.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bundesliga, other top European leagues call for major FIFA reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffe4fd89fab3f8599c026406abfec4875d1753b020ecd19d4ca47b5ed6de40d2</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717--3029f0ff55b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-other-top-european-leagues-call-for-major-fifa-reforms/a-79431717?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundesliga and three other leading European football leagues have said major reforms to world-governing body FIFA are "essential." However, they stopped short of calling for the resignation of boss Gianni Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>After several difficult years, economists now expect German economy to grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:728c576a7f12a8834514cfddf9b77cfcef6da8f4e2ffac8155b3bf5b224f1582</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591--9a99d252976e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economy is growing again, but recovery remains on shaky ground. High government spending is keeping the economy afloat, while energy prices, a shortage of skilled workers and debt continue to weigh on it.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbccf9af32cdf63c9de6475900a5f472f85406f291fd41048d07be45ce9b4c0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
